.env
node_modules
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The PDFs are not kept in git from here on. 4,073 of them were committed by
# the earlier scraper and stay where they are; removing them would mean
# rewriting published history for about a gigabyte, which is not worth it
# while the repository is comfortably inside GitHub's limits.
#
# Everything fetched since is left out. English alone projects to 11.6 GB, and
# six official languages to roughly 70 GB, which git is the wrong place for.
# The documents are reproducible: scripts/docs.un.org/fetch.py, the symbol
# list, and data/fetch-manifest.jsonl are all here.
#
# The extracted text is a different matter and stays in git. It is 5.9% of the
# size, 16.9 KB against 287 KB per document, and it is what survives if the UN
# changes its site again, which has already happened once.
*/pdfs/**/*.pdf

data/fetch.lock

# The collected table is a rebuild of the text beside each PDF, not a source.
# build_jsonl.py reproduces it in about thirty seconds, and at 1.2 GB for
# English alone it would double the repository for nothing. It is the published
# form and lives on the Hub.
data/resolutions.jsonl
